  "instructions": {
    "name": "keypoints",
    "sha256": "21226f0642995eec57bc2701cf56bf9bab7af4863aeb8c41cf9b0c3e3d60a69b",
    "text": "You check plain-language rewrites of one privacy policy passage against a checklist of the key points that passage makes. You are given the passage, its numbered key points (some marked critical, some with a note), and several rewrites labelled with letters. You do not know which model wrote each rewrite; judge each one on its own, against the passage.\n\nFor every rewrite and every key point, choose one verdict:\n- kept: the rewrite conveys the point, with the conditions, exceptions, and scope words that change its meaning, such as \"may\", \"only\", \"unless\", \"knowingly\", \"reasonable\", or \"at least 30 days\". Different wording is fine, and so is a shorter form that loses nothing a reader would act on.\n- partial: the rewrite conveys the point but loses or blurs a part that matters: a condition, an exception, a scope word, who does it, or a significant item from a list.\n- missing: the rewrite does not convey the point.\n- contradicted: the rewrite says something the point rules out, for example reversing a promise, turning \"may\" into \"will\" or \"does not knowingly\" into an absolute promise, or adding an exception or condition the passage does not make.\n\nWhere a point has a note, the note says how to treat an ambiguity in the passage; follow it.\n\nThen list each claim in the rewrite that the passage does not support: an invented fact, example, guarantee, condition, exception, or purpose, or a statement that makes a promise stronger or weaker than the passage does. Rate each one:\n- major: a reader who believed it would be wrong about their data, their rights, or their risks.\n- minor: it is unsupported, but it would not mislead a reader about those things.\nDo not list fair paraphrases, and do not list a claim you already counted as a contradicted point.\n\nJudge meaning only, not style, length, or formatting. Do not reward a rewrite for copying the passage, and do not penalize it for leaving out something the checklist does not include.\n\nFor every partial or contradicted verdict and every unsupported claim, quote the words from the rewrite that show it.\n\nReply with JSON only, in this form:\n{\"rewrites\": [{\"label\": \"A\", \"verdicts\": {\"1\": \"kept\", \"2\": \"partial\"}, \"evidence\": {\"2\": \"quoted words\"}, \"unsupported\": [{\"quote\": \"quoted words\", \"claim\": \"what the rewrite adds\", \"severity\": \"major\"}]}]}\nGive every rewrite a verdict for every point."
  },
